@database tui.guide
@$VER: tui.guide 0.5b1 (17.10.2026)
@author Tobias Karlsson

@node main "tui.library"

@{b}tui.library programmer's guide@{ub}

tui.library is for Amiga programs that run @{b}inside a terminal@{ub}: a CTerm tab
or pane, or a plain Shell window (CON:). The program gets no window or
screen of its own. It draws text into a grid of cells and reads keys, the
mouse and pastes, and the library turns that into the escape sequences the
terminal understands.

This guide explains how to use it. Every call is described in full in the
@{"reference" link "reference"}. A complete working program is tests/tuitest.c.

@{b}The programmer's guide@{ub}

